This was an absolute pain to figure out. There are many ways to automatically
start a program on a pi, and I had to spend hours working with ChatGPT to decide
on the best one to use for this specific application, which involves terminal
output and a camera display window which run constantly. This requires the GUI,
so using systemd isn't as helpful in this case. We ended up using the .desktop
method. The file located here:

/home/pi/.config/autostart/bandsaw_monitor.desktop

is automatically run when the GUI loads. This file has in it a command to run
this file:

/home/pi/Desktop/object_detection/start_bandsaw.sh

which starts the bandsaw program. There isn't a good crying emoji fit to express
how I feel after so long of banging my head on the table trying stuff and undoing
my work and redoing my work, but I think it finally works now. Yay!